= Boris Kamkov

Kamkov (1885-1938) is the Left SR leader and its expert on the village. He will be the loudest voice against the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk.

- @action
- @root: Return to main

@action
title: Against the Treaty
subtitle: Kamkov rallies anti-Brest feeling among the soldiers and the peasants.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and dix >= 20 and dix <= 40
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next advisor action. ?][? if not (dix >= 20 and dix <= 40) : The treaty is not yet in question, or is long settled. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 6;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
Q.month_actions += 1;
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 4, peasants: 3}); Q.anti_brest = (Q.anti_brest || 0) + 1; RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: -3}); RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
!}

Kamkov denounced the peace as a betrayal of the German workers and of the revolutionary war. The soldiers cheered. Lenin did not.

